.git

# The tests need the offline throwaway issuer, which this image is deliberately
# built without, and a container has no reason to carry them.
*_test.go

# NOTE for anyone comparing this with the Python sibling, which excludes
# local_identity.py here: in Go the offline issuer cannot be fenced off by
# leaving a file out, because a Go build with a missing source file fails at
# image-build time rather than failing closed at run time. The `offline` build
# tag does that job instead -- the Dockerfile builds without it, so
# DIAGRID_QUICKSTART_IDENTITY=local on a container derived from this quickstart
# refuses to start rather than quietly turning authentication off. The compiler
# is the guard; prose would be a weaker one.
